{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1637","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"H. Minimize Inversions Number"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a permutation $$$p$$$ of length $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can choose any subsequence, remove it from the permutation, and insert it at the beginning of the permutation keeping the same order."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For every $$$k$$$ from $$$0$$$ to $$$n$$$, find the minimal possible number of inversions in the permutation after you choose a subsequence of length exactly $$$k$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 50\\,000$$$) — the number of test cases."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains one integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 5 \\cdot 10^5$$$) — the length of the permutation."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains the permutation $$$p_1, p_2, \\ldots, p_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le p_i \\le n$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the total sum of $$$n$$$ doesn't exceed $$$5 \\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case output $$$n + 1$$$ integers. The $$$i$$$-th of them must be the answer for the subsequence length of $$$i - 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n1\n1\n4\n4 2 1 3\n5\n5 1 3 2 4\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0 0\n4 2 2 1 4\n5 4 2 2 1 5\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For the length $$$0$$$: $$$[4, 2, 1, 3] \\rightarrow [4, 2, 1, 3]$$$: $$$4$$$ inversions. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For the length $$$1$$$: $$$[4, 2, \\mathbf{1}, 3] \\rightarrow [1, 4, 2, 3]$$$: $$$2$$$ inversions. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For the length $$$2$$$: $$$[4, \\mathbf{2}, \\mathbf{1}, 3] \\rightarrow [2, 1, 4, 3]$$$, or $$$[4, 2, \\mathbf{1}, \\textbf{3}] \\rightarrow [1, 3, 4, 2]$$$: $$$2$$$ inversions. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For the length $$$3$$$: $$$[4, \\mathbf{2}, \\mathbf{1}, \\mathbf{3}] \\rightarrow [2, 1, 3, 4]$$$: $$$1$$$ inversion. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" For the length $$$4$$$: $$$[\\mathbf{4}, \\mathbf{2}, \\mathbf{1}, \\mathbf{3}] \\rightarrow [4, 2, 1, 3]$$$: $$$4$$$ inversions. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"H","problemCode":"1637H","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1637/problem/H"}